Subject: Valid DKIM but strict DMARC alignment failure (adkim=s)
Message-ID: <%MESSAGEID%>

This mail has a valid DKIM signature (rsa-sha256 + ed25519-sha256),
but the DKIM signing domain (d=%DKIM-DOMAIN%) does not exactly match
the From domain (%FROM_ADDRESS%).

With relaxed DMARC alignment (adkim=r, the default), this would pass
because both domains share the same organizational domain.

With strict DMARC alignment (adkim=s), the d= tag must exactly match
the From domain -- a subdomain is not sufficient. This mail should
therefore be rejected by a server enforcing adkim=s.